# Selection lane, 2026-10-28: the oneworld arms of selow1 again, with the fix. selow1's ow1 and owwt were not a test:
# inrun seeded the births' stream from the world, so every colony with the same carry in the one world ran the same
# run (1-2 distinct outcomes a round; all died out at round 23 / 15). inrun sseed= (colsel passes each colony its own)
# fixes it. Same lines otherwise, against clean1 k3, and the same DECIDING MEASURE, named before the first launch:
# garden starvation at round 47, paired by colony against k3's round-47 garden (a colony missing from the garden counts
# as the worse of its pair), two-sided sign test, Bonferroni over 5 arms (p < 0.01). Guards: garden nest and alive.
# Mechanism check: distinct outcomes per round (must be ~32, not 1-2) and the training round's starvation rank against
# the same colonies' garden starvation.
ow2 colsel 31 lex+spoil+crater+shape+scale+lab 32 48 200000 assets/minds/std_pool.txt lesson=scratch/inrun/genomes/c1.raw.txt:0.1 food=mix cg_every=8 labgate=50 labscens=lab_far_mix,lab_far200_fruit labcase=lab_herbs patches=20000:40:120 scalegate=50 setenv=PP_BED_W=448,PP_MIND_DOOR_OPEN=drop scaleopen=1 nestneed=6,3,1 elite=1 kpm=0.003 oneworld=1
owwt2 colsel 31 lex+spoil+crater+shape+scale+lab 32 48 200000 assets/minds/std_pool.txt lesson=scratch/inrun/genomes/c1.raw.txt:0.1 food=mix cg_every=8 labgate=50 labscens=lab_far_mix,lab_far200_fruit labcase=lab_herbs patches=20000:40:120 scalegate=50 setenv=PP_BED_W=448,PP_MIND_DOOR_OPEN=drop scaleopen=1 nestneed=6,3,1 elite=1 kpm=0.003 oneworld=1 weights=spoil:0,crater:0.5,shape:0.5,scale:2,lab:3
